# Azure deployment policy

- **Staging**: Pushing to `staging` deploys the staging app (`azure-deploy-staging.yml`). Use this for testing. This does **not** update `main`.
- **Main vs staging**: `main` and `staging` may differ until a production deploy. Do not auto-sync them on every staging push.
- **Production**: The workflow **Deploy to Azure Production** is **manual-only**. When run, it **merges `staging` into `main`, pushes `main`, then builds and deploys**—so production matches the tested staging tip at deploy time.
- Do not assume the user wants production updated; run or mention the manual workflow only when they ask to deploy to production.
- Optional: **Sync main from staging (manual only)** workflow updates `main` from `staging` without deploying (rare; production deploy already syncs first).
